// yet it reported "user directory not writable", and nothing in the system had a UI to fix it.
//
// # Why the kernel implements it rather than a system service
//
// The grant state **is permission.Registry's own state**. Delegating it to a service would hand
// "who can change the system's dangerous permissions" to a package that can be replaced, while perm.permission.admin's
// bar (SYSTEM_ONLY + PLATFORM + platform-release signature) exists precisely so it can't be replaced.
